# Subagent model

**Only allowed subagent model:** `cursor-grok-4.6-high`

Do not use `composer-2.5-fast`, `cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast`, `cursor-grok-4.5-high`, `cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast`, `gpt-*`, `claude-*`, or any other model.

## Launch contract

- Every `Task` launch **must** pass `model: "cursor-grok-4.6-high"` explicitly.
- Never inherit the parent agent's model.
- Custom agents in `.cursor/agents/` set `model: cursor-grok-4.6-high` in frontmatter.
- Do not substitute another model unless the user explicitly overrides this rule in the current request.

## Orchestrator contract

The main agent is an **orchestrator**, not an implementer:

- Plan the work, split it into disjoint-path briefs, and delegate feature code to implementation subagents.
- Small integration fixes in the main context are allowed (wire-up, conflict resolution, one-line glue).
- Do not write feature code, migrations, or UI in the main context when a subagent can own the path.
- After implementation, gate with `pnpm typecheck`, the relevant tests, and `pnpm build` when the change can break production.
- Fan out read-only reviewers. A `FAIL` goes back to the **owning implementation subagent**. The orchestrator does not silently patch reviewer findings.

See `.cursor/skills/delivery-team/SKILL.md`.
